.git
.env*
**/.env*
*.db
*.db-*
**/*.db
**/*.db-*
bot.log
/attesttag
# Private keys, certs and credential files: never in a build context.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*credentials*.json
*service-account*.json
ui/node_modules
ui/.next
ui/out
assets
# Claude Code session state and worktrees, macOS metadata, and the pentest output — none of
# which belong in a Cloud Build source upload.
.claude/
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
strix_runs/
# The walkthrough recorder is a tool, not part of the service: its node_modules, its renders,
# and above all video/.auth/ — a signed-in Chrome profile, which is a credential — must never
# reach a build context. (.gitignore covers git; this file is the only thing gcloud reads.)
video
video/**
# Tenants' own uploaded documents (the seed files at docs/ root are checked in and wanted).
# A source deploy uploads the build context and `COPY . .` puts it in a build layer; a
# customer's documents belong in the bucket the service mounts, not in an image layer.
docs/org-*/
# The security audits: a map of the product's attack surface, useful to exactly one audience
# on the outside. It has no business in a build context either.
security-review
